<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Indrayudha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">late 8th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Indrayudha was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannauj">Kannauj</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in the late 8th century, the first known ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayudha-dynasty">Ayudha dynasty</a>. The Jain Harivamsha of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jinasena">Jinasena</a>, dated 783, names him as ruling in the north. Caught between the rival Pala, Gurjara-Pratihara and Rashtrakuta powers, he was deposed by the Pala king Dharmapala, who installed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chakrayudha">Chakrayudha</a> in his place.</p></div>
